WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.645
Two camps exist.

00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:07.371
The frequentist Graphical Lasso traces the whole
solution path as lambda varies,

00:00:07.451 --> 00:00:11.096
but returns only point estimates.

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:14.821
The Bayesian Graphical Lasso gives a full posterior
and a marginal likelihood,

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:18.547
but relies on Gibbs samplers that mix poorly and
must restart for every lambda.

00:00:18.627 --> 00:00:22.272
Variational inference could bridge them,

00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:25.997
yet the usual mean-field trick assumes independence,

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:29.723
exactly what a graphical model seeks.

00:00:29.803 --> 00:00:33.448
We need a family that respects dependence and
flexes across lambda and the norm.
